## Concrete correction found

The prep candidate passed a `const mbedtls_ssl_config *` to the pinned public
getter, whose actual declaration accepts a non-const pointer. An expected
`-Werror=discarded-qualifiers` compile rejection proves that mismatch. Only the
new frozen candidate copy adds an explicit cast for this read-only public getter;
no config field or private layout is accessed by production candidate code.
The original prep module and report are retained unchanged. Actual Xtensa
compilation of all real includes/declarations is still required.

## Runtime groups

1. Callback result and original ordering, occupied user-data preservation,
   failed attach without marker, unlabelled and nested unrelated configurations,
   exactly one loan, zeroing, 32 cleanup/reopen/reset cycles.
2. Exact SDK setup failure at TX/transform/session/handshake allocation,
   checksum failure after allocation, rejection before RX allocation, rollback
   pointer clearing and reserve return, final free and repeated cleanup, ledger
   balance.
3. Normal dispatcher and ordinary free pairing, busy fallback through the whole
   canonical reclaim wrapper with SDK-first NULL/release/retry, zero/overflow
   arguments, ISR no-reserve path, canonical bind/detach. Heap and input storage
   are explicit host seams.
4. Simultaneous pthread setup of two independent eligible contexts (exactly one
   slot), then release blocked before erase while a second context must use heap.
   Storage can be loaned again only after the erase provider completes.

Exact semantic controls detect omitted marker admission, omitted loan exclusion,
premature FREE publication, omitted setup rollback release, accidental ordinary
heap free of the reserved pointer, and bypass of canonical reclaim fallback.
The final premature-publication mutant is **phase scoped**: its changed state
assignment is armed only during the erase-barrier scenario. Outside that phase
it preserves ordinary initialization/release, allowing the named ownership
assertion to observe the ordering defect. This scope must not be described as a
fully active mutant across every earlier setup.

